config BR2_PACKAGE_GA_VIBE_ADDONS
	bool "ga-vibe-addons (vendored Greenautarky addon repo snapshot)"
	default y
	help
	  Clones the public greenautarky/vibe_addons addon repository at
	  build time and vendors a snapshot (with .git) into the rootfs at
	  /usr/share/ga/vibe_addons/.

	  ga-bootstrap copies this to the writable data partition on first
	  boot (/mnt/data/supervisor/ga-vibe-addons/, visible to the
	  Supervisor at /data/ga-vibe-addons/) and registers it with the
	  Supervisor as a `file:///data/ga-vibe-addons` store repo. That
	  makes first-boot addon install offline-deterministic, pins the
	  addon-set to the OS release (no `vibe_addons` HEAD drift), and
	  leaves the URL stable for ga_manager-driven future updates
	  (`git fetch origin` inside the writable copy + `ha store reload`).
